    "result_text": "The people import box is in place, and all 4 acceptance tests in `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts` pass when run with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**Server:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/import` (defined in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/import.POST.yml`), takes `{\"text\": \"...\"}`. Its steps match the person form's add:\n- A viewer is refused, and so is an archived sheet.\n- `ValidateImport` then checks every line before anything is stored. Each line is `name,grade,terms,contact`, and the last two may be missing or blank. Each line gets exactly the person form's rules. A name already used as a name or alias anywhere in the sheet's tree is refused, as is a contact already on the sheet. A name or contact repeated within the paste is refused too, ignoring case.\n- If any line fails, the response is a 400 naming that line, and nothing is stored or written to the audit file.\n- Blank lines are skipped, and a paste with no lines at all is refused.\n- If every line passes, `AddImportedPeople` adds each person in order. Each one writes the same `PERSON_ADDED` record as the form, followed by its own `ROLLUP` line, which is the order the test expects. The response is `{\"added\": n}`.\n\nTo share the form's rules, I moved its checks from `ValidatePerson` into a new helper class, `PersonRules`, and the form now calls it too. I had to do this because OfficeFloor refuses to start when a step class has more than one public method, and a static method counts.\n\n**Front end:** `features/people/import.slot.tsx` adds the box below the person form. It has `import-people`, `import-submit`, `import-added` and `import-error`, and it works like the existing claims paste box. Pressing Import clears the old count and any old error, and the count or error appears when the server answers.",
